-- CF-247 API v3 field dictionary: the destination action loaded (REQ-76; Platform Admin 17 Nov 2026 13:12, S2-Build step 1; admin design
-- DESTINATION-DATA-UI-AND-INGESTION-SPEC.md section 2.3).
-- Replaces: nothing (20261116110000 keeps the sync and drift functions; this file only loads the next reviewed list)
-- Retires: nothing
--
-- docs/api/v3/field-dictionary.json now lists the 72 destination fields of each v3 API (moved from pending_fields, where they waited since the
-- schema pack of 17 Nov) and the two G-1 career outcome fields of each API (geography_level, state_code; migration 20261117050000): 1,923 + 148 = 2,071
-- fields. The sync upserts on (api_surface, version, endpoint, field_path), writes only what changed, never deletes, and marks deprecated a field no
-- longer listed (none here: the new list holds every field of the old one). Two reference fields stay pending (array<number> is not an allowed type).
-- Only ref.api_field_dictionary is written: no consumer API object is touched (G3). G1: no job. G2: no setting.

set local lock_timeout = '5s'; -- fixed: lock wait guard for the dictionary writes below

-- Load the reviewed list (docs/api/v3/field-dictionary.json in its compact form, written between the markers by
-- node scripts/api-v3-field-dictionary.mjs embed: each description once; each field
-- [surface w/z/s, endpoint, field_path, data_type, is_nullable 1/0, description index, allowed_values or 0, req_ids or 0])
do $load$
declare
  c jsonb;
  r jsonb;
begin
  c := (
$fields$
